    "CLAUDE.md": "# My wiki\n\nOne person's file-based wiki. Each folder named under `domains` in `dotoriwiki.yaml` is one domain with its own `CLAUDE.md`. Rules every domain follows are in `_schema/common-rules.md`.\n\nYou read this file for two jobs.\n\n- Routing one memo. Pick the domain it belongs to.\n- A question that spans domains. Read each domain's `wiki/index.md` first and open only the pages you need.\n\n## How to route\n\nGo in order and stop at the first match.\n\n1. Feelings, the day, people, plans with friends, thoughts about myself: `journal`.\n2. Something to do, watch, or read later, or a bare link with no comment: `someday`.\n3. Something I tried and learned, at work or on my own, even if it is technical: `learning`.\n4. Nothing fits for sure: `journal`, with low confidence.\n",
    "_schema/common-rules.md": "# Rules for every domain\n\n## Folders\n\n- `raw/` holds the memos, one file each. Never edit or delete them.\n- `raw/<id>.source.md` holds the article or transcript a memo links to. Never edit it either.\n- `wiki/` holds the pages you keep.\n- `wiki/answers/` holds saved chat answers. Do not build on them.\n- `wiki/index.md` and `wiki/log.md` are written by the server. Read them only.\n- `wiki/_review.md` collects judgment calls for me to look at later.\n\n## Page frontmatter\n\n```yaml\ntype: <one of this domain's page types>\nsummary: One line. It goes into index.md as is\naliases: [other names]\nstatus: active | outdated | disputed\nsources: [memo ids]\nupdated: 2026-10-29\n```\n\n## How to work a memo\n\n1. Read the memo and its `.source.md`.\n2. Decide first: a new page, a change to an existing page, a conflict, or nothing to keep.\n3. Before making a page, look for the same subject in `index.md` and every page's `aliases`. Change that page if it exists.\n4. Rewrite a fact that changed instead of appending to it.\n5. Put conflicts and unsure calls in `_review.md`, and mark the page `status: disputed`.\n6. Do not invent facts. Every claim names the memo ids it comes from.\n\n## Links\n\n- Link pages with `[[Page name]]`. Do not link to a page that does not exist.\n- A page in another domain is `[[domain/wiki/Page name]]`.\n",
    "dotoriwiki.yaml": "# This wiki's settings. darami reads this file whenever it needs them, so a saved change\n# applies without a restart. A mistake pauses filing until you fix it. Memos you send in the\n# meantime wait in inbox/. The app shows the problem in Settings, in the folder step, and as a\n# badge on the Memo tab.\n# The model is not set here. Pick it in the app's Settings.\nversion: 1\n\n# Language of the prompts darami sends and the pages it writes: en or ko.\nlocale: en\n\n# Time zone for the dates the wiki writes, such as ledger lines and `updated`.\ntime_zone: America/Chicago\n\n# Where a memo goes when the classifier cannot pick a domain. It waits there for you to confirm.\nfallback_domain: journal\n\n# One entry per domain. The key is the folder name, and that folder's CLAUDE.md tells the\n# model what the domain is for. `description` is what the classifier routes by.\n# `agents_may_read` comes from dotoriwiki. darami checks it but does not use it.\n# `model_profile` comes from dotoriwiki. darami checks it but does not use it.\ndomains:\n  journal:\n    description: My days, the people in them, and what I make of it all\n    page_types:\n      me:\n        description: How I tend to think and act. Exactly one page\n        example: Me.md\n      person:\n        description: One person. What they like, what we did, what they told me\n        example: people/Sam.md\n      theme:\n        description: A thought or worry that keeps coming back\n        example: themes/Work and rest.md\n  learning:\n    description: What I learned by doing it myself, at work or on my own\n    agents_may_read: true\n    page_types:\n      concept:\n        description: One idea. What I understood, what I tried, what confused me\n        example: RAG.md\n      case:\n        description: A situation, what I tried, how it went, the lesson\n        example: cases/Writing agenda items as questions.md\n      project:\n        description: One project. Goal, decisions and why, what I learned\n        example: projects/dotoriwiki.md\n  someday:\n    description: Things to watch, read, or try later, and ideas not yet started\n    page_types:\n      item:\n        description: One thing to do later\n        example: items/LLM agents lecture.md\n      idea:\n        description: A thought that is not a task yet. Related memos gather here\n        example: ideas/Budget app.md\n\n# `feeds` comes from dotoriwiki. darami checks it but collects no news.\n",
